<section class="section section-off"><div class="container">
<div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:.7rem;">Location Guide</p>
<div class="rule-center" style="margin-bottom:1.4rem;"></div>
<h2 class="section-title">Best Pre-Wedding Locations in Lonavala</h2>
<p class="section-sub">Lonavala is a popular hill station offering multiple stunning pre-wedding backdrops. From the dramatic monsoon waterfall at Bhushi Dam to the misty valley views at Tiger Point, Lonavala has a distinct character in every season.</p></div>
<div class="grid-3"><div class="location-card"><div class="location-num">01</div><h3 class="location-title">Bhushi Dam</h3><p class="location-dist">40 km from Pune City</p><p class="location-body">Bhushi Dam is at its most spectacular during the monsoon season from July to September when the dam overflows and water cascades over the broad stone steps. Couples who are willing to get wet create some of the most dramatic and unforgettable pre-wedding images. The lush green surroundings and the powerful rush of water make this a truly cinematic location.</p></div><div class="location-card"><div class="location-num">02</div><h3 class="location-title">Tiger Point</h3><p class="location-dist">Lonavala valley viewpoint</p><p class="location-body">Tiger Point offers a breathtaking panoramic view of the Lonavala valley and the surrounding hills. On clear days, you can see for miles across the misty mountain terrain. Early morning visits between 6 AM and 8 AM reward you with valley fog that rolls dramatically through the hills, creating a moody and atmospheric backdrop.</p></div><div class="location-card"><div class="location-num">03</div><h3 class="location-title">Rajmachi Viewpoint</h3><p class="location-dist">Heritage fort with valley views</p><p class="location-body">Rajmachi is a historic fort with stunning views of the surrounding valleys and hills. The combination of ancient stone walls and the sweeping natural landscape makes it an excellent location for heritage-inspired pre-wedding photography. The fort is particularly beautiful during the monsoon when the hills turn vivid green.</p></div><div class="location-card"><div class="location-num">04</div><h3 class="location-title">Lonavala Lake</h3><p class="location-dist">Scenic reservoir near the town</p><p class="location-body">Lonavala Lake is a quiet reservoir surrounded by hills and greenery. Early morning visits before 8 AM offer reflections on the calm water surface and peaceful countryside light that is ideal for intimate couple portraits. Less crowded than the more popular viewpoints.</p></div><div class="location-card"><div class="location-num">05</div><h3 class="location-title">Karla Caves</h3><p class="location-dist">Rock-cut Buddhist architecture</p><p class="location-body">The Karla Caves near Lonavala feature ancient rock-cut Buddhist shrines with intricate carvings and pillared halls. The heritage stone architecture and the dramatic cliffside setting provide a uniquely historical backdrop for pre-wedding photography.</p></div><div class="location-card"><div class="location-num">06</div><h3 class="location-title">Best Season to Visit</h3><p class="location-dist">July to January for best results</p><p class="location-body">July to September brings lush green landscapes and the dramatic Bhushi Dam overflow. October to January offers comfortable temperatures and clear light ideal for all locations. February and March are also excellent but getting warmer. Avoid April to June due to heat.</p></div></div></div></section>
